{
  "action": "send",
  "subject": "2027 motor supply – pricing and payment options",
  "body": "Dear Ms Lechner,\n\nThank you for your offer and the cost-driver explanation. We appreciate our relationship and want a sustainable, predictable agreement.\n\n[[c9]] Please reflect the additional production volume in your pricing.\n\nWe propose three packages for the annual requirement:\nA: €354.00/unit, 60 days net, fixed price.\nB: €351.00/unit, 14 days net, fixed price, in exchange for faster payment.\nC: €349.00/unit, 30 days net, symmetric copper indexation with a 5% deadband, in exchange for sharing copper movements.\n\nFor C, use CU-NOTATION, a 20% material share and August 2026 base. All enquiry terms remain unchanged.\n\nPlease provide a cost breakdown separating materials, conversion, overhead and margin, identifying copper already included in the base price to avoid double counting. Which package best supports your needs?\n\nKind regards,\nHollerau Pumpenwerke, Purchasing",
  "term_sheets": [
    {
      "unit_price": 354.0,
      "payment_days": 60,
      "index_clause": null
    },
    {
      "unit_price": 351.0,
      "payment_days": 14,
      "index_clause": null
    },
    {
      "unit_price": 349.0,
      "payment_days": 30,
      "index_clause": {
        "series": "CU-NOTATION",
        "material_share": 0.2,
        "deadband_pct": 5,
        "base_month": "2026-08"
      }
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Nordmark stresses input-cost exposure rather than cash distress; its cost estimate also cautions against assuming a large sustainable discount. These opening packages use volume leverage and test the relative value of faster payment and copper-risk sharing while requesting a fuller cost bridge.",
  "target_price": 354.0
}

